{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum","id":1090554,"title":"Acanthus and Forces Arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-09T19:10:23-07:00","id":1090554,"title":"Acanthus and Forces Arcanum","content":"&quot;Lightning arrives at its appointed time in the tale, not before. In Arcadia, elemental powers are visible manifestations of destiny and Fae passions. Fire isn\u2019t heat alone, but the anger of the Fair Folk or the climax of an apocalyptic myth; it is not to be raised through some mechanistic act of will.&quot; p. 21, MtA 2e<br /> <br /> I sort of get how Forces is the Acanthus' inferior Arcanum, but I'm still struggling to wrap my head around this. In your own words, why is this so? Any instances where an Acanthus in your game struggled with Forces? Any unexpected outcomes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T20:03:15-07:00","id":1090569,"title":"","content":"The Acanthus's &quot;Mystery card&quot; in the Tarot is the Wheel of Fortune, and the card that represents the Path's members is the Fool; as the nature of their Awakening suggests, the thematic niche they occupy is one of maneuvering themselves or their targets for the right angle with an eye toward the knock-on effects of a given decision \u2014 the greater powers of the Forces Arcanum are both too unsubtle and too far-spreading for a subtype of mage whose natural talents lie in shifting how attractive a given course of action is without actually outright preventing it.<br /> <br /> The movements that permeate the cosmos are grand in scale and coarsely-grained in immediate appeal; mages on the Path of Thorns deal in the personal and the particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T22:32:20-07:00","id":1090596,"title":"","content":"Forces govern things that move under their own rules, not the rules of fairy tales, destinies, and narratives that the Acanthus are accustomed to. At least things like Matter stay where they are, and Life's living creatures have the decency to act out their roles in their destinies! (Meanwhile, the Moros and Thyrsus next door are sighing)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T01:36:22-07:00","id":1090636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1090596#post1090596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces govern things that move under their own rules, not the rules of fairy tales, destinies, and narratives that the Acanthus are accustomed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the best pithy summary I've heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T00:59:09-07:00","id":1091007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1090569#post1090569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Acanthus's &quot;Mystery card&quot; in the Tarot is the Wheel of Fortune, and the card that represents the Path's members is the Fool; as the nature of their Awakening suggests, the thematic niche they occupy is one of maneuvering themselves or their targets for the right angle with an eye toward the knock-on effects of a given decision \u2014 the greater powers of the Forces Arcanum are both too unsubtle and too far-spreading for a subtype of mage whose natural talents lie in shifting how attractive a given course of action is without actually outright preventing it.<br /> <br /> The movements that permeate the cosmos are grand in scale and coarsely-grained in immediate appeal; mages on the Path of Thorns deal in the personal and the particular.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bVery well said <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. Thanks for sharing your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:03:32-07:00","id":1091009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1090596#post1090596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces govern things that move under their own rules, not the rules of fairy tales, destinies, and narratives that the Acanthus are accustomed to. At least things like Matter stay where they are, and Life's living creatures have the decency to act out their roles in their destinies! (Meanwhile, the Moros and Thyrsus next door are sighing)</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly. Acanthus just can't coax lightning to work quite like the other Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T00:57:19-07:00","id":1095051,"title":"","content":"Personally, I see it as Forces being an Arcanum that needs outright and brutal command to effectively wield, which is why Obrimoi can wield it easily, they needed that kind of might to Awaken. Acanthi, however, tend to work more subtly. They nudge and motivate others to move where they want them to go, but Forces simply can't be nudged along, it'll just spill everywhere otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1090569#post1090569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the card that represents the Path's members is the Fool; as the nature of their Awakening suggests.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a minor gripe of mine, so please don't take what I'm gonna say next too awfully seriously, but that is wrong. The common stereotype of the Fool relying on luck and destiny is a merely a branch off the card's core meaning, which is beginnings and possibilities. The Fool is a blank slate, about to begin their journey through the other cards (hence the bindle). The common imagery of heading off the cliff is more align with going down the rabbit hole than relying on fate to catch you, which is why other depictions have the Fool in the middle of a crossroads. Another way to depict it would be the part where Morpheus offers the blue and red pills to Neo (and would actually be a more accurate depiction than a cliff or crossroads).<br /> <br /> \u200bTo summarize, The Fool is much more appropriate for the Awakening itself than one of the Paths, in fact, one Path in particular would be flying in the face of the card's meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T01:15:16-07:00","id":1095056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1095051#post1095051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is a minor gripe of mine, so please don't take what I'm gonna say next too awfully seriously, but that is wrong. The common stereotype of the Fool relying on luck and destiny is a merely a branch off the card's core meaning, which is beginnings and possibilities. The Fool is a blank slate, about to begin their journey through the other cards (hence the bindle). The common imagery of heading off the cliff is more align with going down the rabbit hole than relying on fate to catch you, which is why other depictions have the Fool in the middle of a crossroads. Another way to depict it would be the part where Morpheus offers the blue and red pills to Neo (and would actually be a more accurate depiction than a cliff or crossroads).<br /> <br /> \u200bTo summarize, The Fool is much more appropriate for the Awakening itself than one of the Paths, in fact, one Path in particular would be flying in the face of the card's meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi there! Fellow Tarot reader here.<br /> <br /> Your statements are reflected in Keys to the Supernal Tarot, a Mage 1e supplement that deals with the Tarot, and how to use it in a Mage game. They have The Fool representing, as you said, the Awakening itself - but also the Arcanum of Time, because as you said The Fool is the beginning of a new journey and a new history. And Time, the Arcanum that grants you the ability to foresee and control Consequences of a Choice, is intrinsically connected to the Path of Thorns whose dual themes are Choice and Consequence.<br /> <br /> And judging by this phrase used by Satchel:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the thematic niche they occupy is one of maneuvering themselves or their targets for the right angle with an eye toward the knock-on effects of a given decision </div> </div> </div>I think that Satchel understands that yes, both The Fool and the Acanthus are manipulators of Choice and Consequence who has the best guess on which rabbit hole leads to which Wonderland, and who has a fairly good idea of which pill lead to which sort of destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:06:12-07:00","id":1095236,"title":"","content":"Also, in Mage, part of the conceit is that popular ideas about Tarot meaning are in fact wrong, or at least heavily distorted.<br /> <br /> Like, there's no fifth suit of mirrors for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T16:54:51-07:00","id":1095660,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> it's good to hear from the contrarian's side. Do you think there's a better card that would fit the Acanthus then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T18:01:06-07:00","id":1095690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1095051#post1095051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is a minor gripe of mine, so please don't take what I'm gonna say next too awfully seriously, but that is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is markedly not, because nobody was talking about &quot;the common stereotype&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>In the Awakened Tarot, the Acanthus personifies the Fool: a trackless soul, able to move freely through the currents of destiny. Witches don\u2019t get to this state through naive wandering, but by unburdening themselves of old attachments, and using magic to slip the grasp of new ones. </b>Their Mysteries involve the Wheel of Fortune, a card depicting the relentless spin of destiny.There\u2019s no still place to stand in the world, no equilibrium to be had. Even Acanthus can\u2019t just grab a spoke of the Wheel to get to a favorable situation. <b>A Witch needs to get to the right place at the right time to nudge things <u>just so</u>.</b> The further she is from the ideal opportunity, the more she needs to push \u2014 with stronger, more dangerous sorcery. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Witches start by breaking patterns</b>, rebelling against destiny with strange choices.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> They see the secret rhythms of their lives, and refuse to dance to the beat. <b>When you don\u2019t do what life expects of you, a stranger world reveals itself</b>.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Arcadia\u2019s fairy lords are living forces of destiny. Don\u2019t drink or eat what they offer. Don\u2019t fall in love or lash out from hate, because you\u2019ll trade your destiny for theirs. <b>There are no trivial acts in the Watchtower of Fate and Time.</b> </div> </div> </div>You have a bunch of people who reached basic enlightenment by acting as though they weren't the people their past and station said they were, had an encounter with the secret nature of reality where one wrong step spelled disaster, and came out of it with a symbolic connection to reflective materials and precise weaponry and the ability to warp history and destiny. That does, in fact, track to &quot;the nature of their Awakening suggests the Path of Thorns works best for people who recognize that a highly complex set of circumstances govern the world and any given action creates ripples in that structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not a suitable proxy for your beefs with pop culture, least of all when you have to mispunctuate my statements to get them anywhere near those gripes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T22:15:33-07:00","id":1095765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1095690#post1095690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a bunch of people who reached basic enlightenment by acting as though they weren't the people their past and station said they were, had an encounter with the secret nature of reality where one wrong step spelled disaster, and came out of it with a symbolic connection to reflective materials and precise weaponry and the ability to warp history and destiny. That does, in fact, track to &quot;the nature of their Awakening suggests the Path of Thorns works best for people who recognize that a highly complex set of circumstances govern the world and any given action creates ripples in that structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not a suitable proxy for your beefs with pop culture, least of all when you have to mispunctuate my statements to get them anywhere near those gripes.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I didn't mispunctuate you to remove context, but to keep my response relevant to the point I was making. Second, while what you're describing is certainly part of The Fool's meaning, but like I said before, it's more of a specific branch to the card's core meaning. I'd personally find the High Priestess to be a more accurate symbol, as it specifically relates to working in subtle ways and being guided by intuition, and she's a seer, too.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you're wondering about the Obrimos having the High Priestess, the thing is, she only has religious beliefs, not religious doctrine. It's like the difference between saying &quot;This is true&quot; and &quot;Truth is relative&quot;. Or, if you've seen Dogma, the difference between beliefs and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T23:45:16-07:00","id":1095777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090554-acanthus-and-forces-arcanum?p=1095765#post1095765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I didn't mispunctuate you to remove context, but to keep my response relevant to the point I was making.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point you were making was that my <i>referencing what the book says</i> was incorrect in the context of <i>understanding what the book says.</i> This thread is not about whether the Awakened Tarot is flush with all interpretations of the Tarot in real-world occult traditions.<br /> <br /> Nobody was suggesting that the Acanthus as presented in 2e fit the pop-cultural reading of The Fool. Your issues with erroneous Tarot readings have nothing to do with anything anyone was talking about here \u2014 it's not a <i>response to</i> the quoted section in any meaningful sense of the word, and I resent being treated as a proxy target for unrelated gripes.<br /> <br /> <br /> To bring this back to the topic, just as the Moros inch toward self-perfection and the Mastigos seek self-mastery, the Acanthus pursue self-determination: being able to pick and choose their place in the world irrespective of their background as though they stepped into existence just yesterday, ready to take advantage of a fresh start. That's not the divinely-inspired intuition of the Priestess or the border-jumping liminality of the Hermit, that's the traveler's mien of the Fool, the perpetual drifter and the new kid in town.<br /> <br /> If their arrival coincides with the post office going up in flames, it's an omen, not an admission of guilt \u2014 coincidence is the worst the Witch has held against them, and it's easier to shrug that off when your part in the arson doesn't have your magical fingerprints on the culprit, much less the crime scene. As has been observed over and over, theirs is the roundabout route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}